 the end of the  emperor kaido and big mom and this  message is driven home even harder when  the narrator corrects his initial  mistake of declaring kite of the victor  the actual victor turns out is luffy on  top of that kaido also finally has  closure in the last chapter realizing  that luffy is indeed joy boy bringing  closure to his big goal of finding  someone strong enough to defeat him  straw hats and the rest of the alliance  are celebrating choppers towards  treating patients good for him including  my man zorro who does seem to be in a  truly dangerous condition right here and  yamato gets the remaining beast pirates  to surrender while momo carries the  whole delegation of the scabbards and  hiori to the flower capital declaring  kaido's defeat and announcing the new  shogun of wano oh also a major shout out  to my man frankie who is the only straw  hat that really looks like he could  still keep easily going after this  respect and so really this entire  chapter is screaming that this fight is  over and the yonko are dead i suppose  and so now the big question here is of  course is that actually true or is oda  sensei throwing us one of his infamous  red herrings here let's think about this  for a second right okay so does it make  actually sense for kaido and big mom two  characters in dire need for some  redemption and closure to die burning to  death painfully in a volcano kaido who  wants nothing more than see joyboy and  die an honorable death and big mom who  has no idea yet that she has been  terrorizing her own people in her  feeding frenzies i do find that kind of  hard to believe i also want to say i  find it a bit suspicious that it wasn't  mount fuji the main volcano of the  island that erupted but onigashima like  a weird angle and the narrator who  wasn't super reliable throughout the  raid either hasn't declared either of  them dead also kaido has a literal file  form as we now know so there's that as  well what i'm getting at here is of 